gcalbert@spam.ua.oz.au (Gregory Calbert) writes:


>I am not sure if this is a bug or not but I have been experiencing
>problems with restoring saved games in NetHack (Version 3.1 I Think).

>Whenever I save a game, and come back to it the next day and restore the
>saved game my inventory gets corrupted

>Is this a BUG? .. has anyone else experienced this?

If you are playing on a MS-DOS PC, and you are playing with the most recent
binary from linc.cis.upenn.edu, then ... yes it is a bug.  Several people
have reported it, and some have even found it.

A new binary is on the way.

The trick for you (and all others) is to restore your game in the *exact*
environment in which it was save (specifically wrt free memory).  The
restore code is currently mucking with saved pointers in a bad way.

So if you play a game with 585932 bytes free make sure that you have
585932 bytes free when you restore (ie no config.sys changes or TSR
changes) and everything will be fine.

